    "checks": [
      "The code has no accessory dwelling unit. No district lists a second unit on a single-family lot, and the residential accessory uses are garages, fences and freestanding structures such as bathhouses, greenhouses and sheds (318.3O)",
      "'No more than one principal use shall be permitted on a lot', except in the Pedestrian-Oriented, Mixed-Use Overlay (401). A building with two or more dwelling units is a multiple-family dwelling (201)",
      "Use variances are barred: 'A variance shall not be granted for any use which is not permitted in the zoning district where the request is being made' (704.6C(2)(d), also 201 'Variance'). The routes left are the listed two-unit uses or a zoning amendment",
      "Duplexes are permitted by right in HR (2,500 sq ft per unit, 50 ft wide) and TC (4,500 sq ft per unit). Building conversion into two or more dwelling units is a special exception only in TC. The units must then meet the garden apartment, townhouse or low-rise apartment rules, and the building's outside may not change except for safety (309.3F, 315.3C)",
      "Up to two apartments on the second or third floor above a nonresidential first floor are permitted by right in TC (309.2FF)",
      "A family is related persons or up to five unrelated persons with one kitchen. Domestic servants are 'an adjunct to the term family' (201)",
      "Freestanding accessory structures: at most 15 ft tall, not in front of the principal building, 10 ft from it and 5 ft from side and rear lines (318.3O(3))",
      "Lot figures for a single-family house: LR 10,000 sq ft, MR 7,500 sq ft, HR and TC 5,000 sq ft (306.6, 307.6, 308.6, 309.6)",
      "A building may go on a nonconforming lot if the yards are met (406.2B)",
      "Parking counts are in Table 6.1, a PDF attachment that was not read. A fraction of 0.25 or more counts as one space (601.1D)",
      "Floodplain rules are in Chapter 8 (8-402)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Quakertown Borough Zoning Officer. Read in a browser on eCode360 (print view), one page at a time, on 2026-11-16. Read: 201 definitions, 306, 307, 308, 309, 315 (on the Part 3 page), 316, 318, Part 4 (401 to 409), 601, 704, Chapter 8 section 402, the New Laws page and code searches. NC and HC were seen only in search snippets (both list single-family houses). Not read: Part 1, 301 to 305, 310 to 314.1 in full, 317, 319 historic preservation, 320, Part 5, 602 to 604, the rest of Part 7, Part 8, Table 3.1 and Table 6.1 (PDFs) and the rest of Chapter 8."
